---
import SoftwareDocsLayout from '../../../layouts/SoftwareDocsLayout.astro';
import DocCallout from '../../../components/docs/DocCallout.astro';
import DocChecklist from '../../../components/docs/DocChecklist.astro';
import DocDecision from '../../../components/docs/DocDecision.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const webstore = 'https://webstore.illinois.edu/shop/CISCO_AnyConnect_VPN.aspx';
const macVPN = 'https://answers.illinois.edu/illinois/47629';
const winVPN = 'https://answers.illinois.edu/illinois/47507';
const macRDP = 'https://answers.uillinois.edu/ahs/142960';
const microsoft = 'https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-app/get-started-connect-devices-desktops-apps?pivots=remote-pc&tabs=macos-pc';
const headings = [['start','Before you start'],['network','Network'],['vpn','Install and connect the VPN'],['mac','Connect from a Mac'],['windows','Connect from Windows'],['work','Start working'],['finish','Save and sign out'],['help','Troubleshooting'],['references','References']];
const toc = headings.map(([id,label])=>({id,label}));
---
<SoftwareDocsLayout title="Remote access · CEE 406" description="Connect to the CEE 406 Windows workstation from a Mac or PC using the Illinois network and Remote Desktop." activeModule="remote-access" toc={toc}>
 <header class="doc-header">
  <span class="doc-header__badge">Class workstation</span>
  <h1 class="doc-header__title">Remote access</h1>
  <p class="doc-header__desc">Use the class Windows workstation from your Mac or PC. All course software is already installed; you control it from your own computer.</p>
 </header>
 <figure class="remote-overview"><img src={`${base}documentation/branding/remote-access-logo.svg`} width="800" height="400" alt="Your computer connects through the Illinois network to the CEE-ALQADI-20 class workstation." decoding="async" /><figcaption>Connect to the Illinois network, then open the remote Windows desktop.</figcaption></figure>
 <section id="start" data-section class="doc-section">
  <h2>Before you start</h2>
  <ul class="doc-list">
   <li><strong>Have your Illinois NetID and password ready.</strong><ul><li>You will also need your enrolled MFA method for VPN sign-in.</li></ul></li>
   <li><strong>Confirm your access with the instructor or TA.</strong><ul><li>Your account must be allowed to use Remote Desktop on this workstation. Class enrollment alone does not configure access.</li><li>Class staff must keep the workstation powered on, connected to the network, and configured for remote access.</li></ul></li>
   <li><strong>Book prolonged sessions in advance.</strong><ul><li>The dedicated workstation allows one connected student at a time.</li><li>Arrange your timeslot with class staff before an extended session, especially when software is needed for an assignment. Confirm the booking method with the instructor or TA.</li></ul></li>
   <li><strong>Use the class connection details.</strong><ul><li>The workstation name is <code>CEE-ALQADI-20</code>.</li><li>Illinois’s published instructions use the AD domain <code>ad.uillinois.edu</code>. If the short name cannot be found, use the full address confirmed by class staff; the standard campus form is <code>CEE-ALQADI-20.ad.uillinois.edu</code>.</li></ul></li>
  </ul>
  <div class="remote-settings">
   <div><span>Computer name</span><code id="remote-host">CEE-ALQADI-20</code><button type="button" data-copy-value="CEE-ALQADI-20" hidden>Copy name</button></div>
   <div><span>Remote Desktop username</span><code>UOFI\yourNetID</code><small>Replace <code>yourNetID</code> with your own NetID.</small></div>
   <p data-copy-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
  </div>
  <DocCallout kind="note" label="Access first"><p>If your account has not been approved, ask class staff before troubleshooting passwords or changing settings. Install the clients on your own computer; students do not need to change the workstation’s firewall or Remote Desktop settings.</p></DocCallout>
  <DocCallout kind="note" label="One student at a time"><p>Book a timeslot before prolonged use. Finish within your agreed time and sign out so the next student can connect. Do not accept a prompt that would disconnect another student.</p></DocCallout>
 </section>
 <section id="network" data-section class="doc-section">
  <h2>Network</h2>
  <DocDecision id="remote-network" label="Where are you connecting from?" choices={[
   {value:'away',label:'Off campus or on another network',title:'Connect the VPN first',body:'Home Wi-Fi, a hotspot, and campus guest Wi-Fi need the Illinois VPN for this direct connection. Keep it connected throughout your session.',href:'#vpn',linkLabel:'Install and connect the VPN →'},
   {value:'campus',label:'IllinoisNet or a campus wired connection',title:'Use your campus connection',body:'Connect to IllinoisNet or a university campus wired network. If the workstation is unreachable, try the Illinois VPN and check with class staff.',href:'#mac',linkLabel:'Continue to Remote Desktop →'},
  ]} />
  <p>This guide uses a direct connection through IllinoisNet or the VPN. Leave the Remote Desktop <strong>Gateway</strong> unset unless class staff give you a different configuration. <a href="https://www.techservices.illinois.edu/services/vpn-essentials/">Illinois VPN guidance</a>.</p>
 </section>
 <section id="vpn" data-section class="doc-section">
  <h2>Install and connect the VPN</h2>
  <p>If Cisco Secure Client is already installed, start at step 4. Older installations may be labeled Cisco AnyConnect.</p>
  <ol class="doc-list">
   <li>Open the <a href={webstore}>Illinois WebStore’s free Urbana VPN offer</a> and sign in.<ul><li>Add the offer to your cart and complete the free order.</li><li>Open <strong>Order History</strong>, select the blue order number, and download the installer for your Mac or Windows computer.</li></ul></li>
   <li>Open the downloaded package and run its installer.<ul><li>On Mac, open the downloaded disk image and its Cisco installer.</li><li>On Windows, right-click the downloaded ZIP and select <strong>Extract All → Extract</strong>. Run the Cisco installer from the extracted folder, rather than inside the ZIP.</li><li>Follow the installer prompts, accept its license agreement, and finish the installation.</li><li>Use your local administrator credentials when requested. On a managed computer, ask your IT support team to install it.</li></ul></li>
   <li>Allow the permissions required by the installer.<ul><li>On Mac, allow the Cisco VPN background service and Socket Filter extension in System Settings when prompted.</li><li>Follow the current <a href={macVPN}>Mac installation guide</a> or <a href={winVPN}>Windows installation guide</a> if a permission or installer screen differs.</li></ul></li>
   <li>Open <strong>Cisco Secure Client</strong> and select the Illinois <strong>Split Tunnel</strong> profile, then <strong>Connect</strong>.<ul><li>If the profile list is empty, enter <code>connect.vpn.illinois.edu</code>. Illinois documents this as the setup address; it connects using Tunnel All and downloads the profiles.</li></ul></li>
   <li>Complete the university sign-in.<ul><li>Use your full email address, <code>yourNetID@illinois.edu</code>, and your NetID password.</li><li>Complete the MFA prompt with your enrolled method, then return to Cisco Secure Client.</li></ul></li>
   <li>Wait until Cisco shows <strong>Connected</strong>.<ul><li>Keep the VPN connected while using the workstation. Next, choose the instructions for your computer below.</li></ul></li>
  </ol>
  <DocCallout kind="tip" label="Two sign-ins"><p>The VPN uses <code>yourNetID@illinois.edu</code>. The remote Windows desktop uses <code>UOFI\yourNetID</code>. Both use your Illinois NetID password.</p></DocCallout>
  <DocDecision id="remote-platform" label="Which computer are you using?" choices={[
   {value:'mac',label:'Mac',title:'Use Windows App',body:'Download Microsoft’s client, add the class PC, and open its Windows desktop.',href:'#mac',linkLabel:'Mac instructions →'},
   {value:'windows',label:'Windows',title:'Use Remote Desktop Connection',body:'The client is included with Windows. Open it and enter the class PC name.',href:'#windows',linkLabel:'Windows instructions →'},
  ]} />
 </section>
 <section id="mac" data-section class="doc-section">
  <h2>Connect from a Mac</h2>
  <ol class="doc-list">
   <li>Install <strong>Windows App</strong> by Microsoft from the Mac App Store.<ul><li>Use the download link in <a href={microsoft}>Microsoft’s Mac connection guide</a>. This replaces the older Microsoft Remote Desktop client.</li></ul></li>
   <li>Open Windows App, select <strong>Devices → + → Add PC</strong>.<ul><li>You can add a remote PC without signing in to Windows App. You do not need a Windows 365 subscription or a workspace feed.</li></ul></li>
   <li>Enter <code>CEE-ALQADI-20</code> in <strong>PC Name</strong>.<ul><li>If the name is not found, use the instructor-confirmed full address described above.</li><li>Use <strong>CEE 406 workstation</strong> as the friendly name. Keep the user account set to ask when needed and leave Gateway unset for this network/VPN workflow.</li></ul></li>
   <li>Select <strong>Add</strong>, then double-click the saved PC.<ul><li>When asked for credentials, enter <code>UOFI\yourNetID</code> and your NetID password.</li><li>If macOS requests local-network access for Windows App, allow it for this connection.</li></ul></li>
   <li>Wait for the Windows desktop.<ul><li>The workstation desktop is your remote session. Open the assigned course software there.</li></ul></li>
  </ol>
  <DocCallout kind="note" label="Check the computer identity"><p>If Windows App shows a certificate or identity warning, verify the destination with class staff before continuing. Do not accept an unexpected computer name.</p></DocCallout>
  <p><a href={macRDP}>Illinois’s Mac Remote Desktop guide</a> documents the campus naming and account format. Its gateway workflow differs from the direct VPN route used here.</p>
 </section>
 <section id="windows" data-section class="doc-section">
  <h2>Connect from Windows</h2>
  <ol class="doc-list">
   <li>Open Start, search for <strong>Remote Desktop Connection</strong>, and open it.<ul><li>Alternatively, press <kbd>Windows</kbd> + <kbd>R</kbd>, type <code>mstsc</code>, and press Enter.</li></ul></li>
   <li>In <strong>Computer</strong>, enter <code>CEE-ALQADI-20</code> and select <strong>Connect</strong>.<ul><li>If the name is not found, use the instructor-confirmed full address described above.</li></ul></li>
   <li>Choose <strong>More choices → Use a different account</strong> if Windows suggests your personal account.<ul><li>Enter <code>UOFI\yourNetID</code> and your NetID password.</li></ul></li>
   <li>Wait for the Windows desktop, then open the assigned course software.<ul><li>These steps follow the university’s <a href="https://answers.illinois.edu/illinois.las/74122">Remote Desktop walkthrough</a>.</li></ul></li>
  </ol>
  <DocCallout kind="note" label="Check the computer identity"><p>If you see a certificate or identity warning, verify the destination with class staff before continuing. Do not disable certificate checks or accept an unexpected computer name.</p></DocCallout>
 </section>
 <section id="work" data-section class="doc-section">
  <h2>Start working</h2>
  <ul class="doc-list">
   <li>Open the software named in your assignment from the remote Start menu or desktop.<ul><li>All software used during CEE 406 is already installed on the dedicated workstation. You do not need to download the course programs there.</li><li>If a program is missing or a license prompt prevents you from working, contact the instructor or TA.</li></ul></li>
   <li>Use the relevant <a href={`${base}documentation/`}>software guide</a> for your homework or project.<ul><li>A file opened or saved inside the remote desktop belongs to the workstation, not automatically to your Mac or PC.</li></ul></li>
   <li>Respect other students’ sessions.<ul><li>Only one student can be connected at a time. Book prolonged sessions in advance and follow your reserved timeslot.</li><li>If Windows warns that another user will be disconnected, cancel and contact class staff.</li></ul></li>
  </ul>
  <DocChecklist id="remote-access-first-session" title="First connection" note="Track your progress here. These checks do not test your network or sign you in." items={[
   'Class staff have confirmed my workstation access.',
   'I have booked a timeslot if I need a prolonged session.',
   'I am on IllinoisNet/campus wired networking, or Cisco shows Connected.',
   'I opened the remote desktop with my own UOFI account.',
   'I can open the assigned course software.',
   'I know where my files are saved and how to retrieve them.',
  ]} />
 </section>
 <section id="finish" data-section class="doc-section">
  <h2>Save and sign out</h2>
  <ol class="doc-list">
   <li>Save your project and results in your own folder on the workstation.<ul><li>Use your NetID in folder and file names where needed to keep class work separate.</li></ul></li>
   <li>Copy the files you need to your own Illinois Box or OneDrive.<ul><li>You can upload through a browser inside the remote desktop. Check the upload before leaving.</li></ul></li>
   <li>Close the course software, then use the remote Windows <strong>Start → account icon → Sign out</strong>.<ul><li>Closing the Remote Desktop window only disconnects; it may leave your programs running.</li><li>Do not shut down or restart the shared workstation.</li></ul></li>
   <li>After signing out, disconnect Cisco Secure Client if you used the VPN.</li>
  </ol>
 </section>
 <section id="help" data-section class="doc-section">
  <h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
  <details><summary>The computer cannot be found or the connection times out</summary><ol class="doc-list"><li>Confirm IllinoisNet or an active Illinois VPN connection.<ul><li>Guest Wi-Fi and home Wi-Fi alone are not the campus connection.</li></ul></li><li>Check the PC name and try the full address confirmed by class staff.<ul><li>The standard Illinois AD suffix is <code>ad.uillinois.edu</code>.</li></ul></li><li>Ask class staff to check workstation power, network access, Remote Desktop settings, and account permissions.</li></ol></details>
  <details><summary>My credentials are rejected or access is denied</summary><ul class="doc-list"><li>Use your own <code>UOFI\yourNetID</code> for Remote Desktop.<ul><li>Check that the saved account is not a personal Windows or Microsoft account.</li></ul></li><li>If credentials work for Illinois services but workstation access is denied, ask class staff to check your Remote Desktop permissions.</li></ul></details>
  <details><summary>Cisco will not connect</summary><ul class="doc-list"><li>Check your internet connection, installed Cisco permissions, and MFA prompt.<ul><li>Follow the <a href={macVPN}>Mac</a> or <a href={winVPN}>Windows</a> installation guide for the exact message.</li></ul></li><li>For VPN problems, contact <a href="mailto:consult@illinois.edu">consult@illinois.edu</a> or <a href="tel:+12172447000">217-244-7000</a>.<ul><li>Report your operating system and the error text. Do not send your password or MFA codes.</li></ul></li></ul></details>
  <details><summary>The desktop is slow, disconnected, or already in use</summary><ul class="doc-list"><li>Keep the VPN connected and use a stable network.<ul><li>For a slow connection, try a smaller remote window or lower resolution in the client’s display settings.</li></ul></li><li>Reconnect to the same workstation with your own account after a dropped connection.</li><li>If another student is using it, contact class staff rather than forcing that student off.</li></ul></details>
  <DocCallout kind="tip" label="Ask the right team"><p>The instructor or TA handles workstation access, software, and class scheduling. Technology Services helps with the Illinois VPN and NetID sign-in.</p></DocCallout>
 </section>
 <section id="references" data-section class="doc-section">
  <h2>References</h2>
  <ul class="doc-list"><li><a href={webstore}>Illinois WebStore: Urbana VPN</a>.</li><li>Illinois Cisco installation: <a href={macVPN}>macOS</a> and <a href={winVPN}>Windows</a>.</li><li><a href={macRDP}>Illinois: Remote Desktop from a Mac</a>.</li><li><a href={microsoft}>Microsoft: Windows App remote PC connections</a>.</li><li><a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-app/user-account-settings-add-remove-manage">Microsoft: Windows App accounts</a>.</li></ul>
  <p class="remote-source-note">Instructions checked October 1, 2026. The workstation name, preinstalled course software, and one-user booking requirement were supplied for CEE 406. Class staff must confirm its full DNS address and your account permissions. This page does not test workstation availability.</p>
 </section>
</SoftwareDocsLayout>
<script>
 document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-copy-value]').forEach(button=>{
  button.hidden=false;
  button.addEventListener('click',async()=>{
   const status=document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-copy-status]');
   try { await navigator.clipboard.writeText(button.dataset.copyValue!); if(status) status.textContent='Computer name copied.'; }
   catch { if(status) status.textContent='Copy CEE-ALQADI-20 from the text above.'; }
  });
 });
</script>
<style>
 .remote-overview { margin: 0 0 2rem; padding: 1rem; border-radius: 12px; background: #eef3f8; }
 .remote-overview img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 18rem; object-fit: contain; }
 .remote-overview figcaption { color: #3e5369; font-size: .8125rem; text-align: center; line-height: 1.5; }
 .remote-settings { padding: 1rem; border: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-radius: 8px; }
 .remote-settings > div { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: .5rem .75rem; margin: .4rem 0 .85rem; }
 .remote-settings span, .remote-settings small { width: 100%; font-size: .8125rem; color: var(--color-text-muted); }
 .remote-settings code { overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
 .remote-settings button { min-height: 44px; padding: .4rem .75rem; border-radius: 6px; border: 1px solid var(--color-border); color: var(--color-text); background: var(--color-surface-alt); font: inherit; font-size: .8125rem; cursor: pointer; }
 .remote-settings button:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--color-accent); outline-offset: 3px; }
 [data-copy-status] { margin: 0; font-size: .8125rem; }
 .remote-source-note { font-size: .8125rem; color: var(--color-text-muted); }
 .doc-section code { overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
 .doc-section details summary { min-height: 44px; padding-block: .75rem; cursor: pointer; font-size: .9rem; }
</style>
